{"title":"Hensel's Lemma","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Hensel's Lemma</b> is a important result in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_Theory\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Number Theory\">Number Theory</a> for solving <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polynomial_congruences\" title=\"Polynomial congruences\">polynomial congruences</a>. It is named after the German mathematician Kurt Hensel, who derived it.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Statement\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Statement</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Uses\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Uses</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Example\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Example</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Introductory\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introductory</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Intermediate\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Olympiad\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Olympiad</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Statement\">Statement</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hensel%27s_Lemma&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Statement\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is a polynomial function with integer coefficients and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be a prime number. Also, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be an arbitrary integer with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17d88e2fdeef66df0e37def936f39b773567278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. Suppose further that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a solution to the congruence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/0/e40afcf9dc7b212575647ec43a0d272a14bdc2e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) \\equiv 0 \\pmod {p^{k-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"22\" />. From here, there are three cases to consider:\n</p>\n<ol><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/c/72cc19e130ba0717b159a2f0822b6ef3796dcc8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> is not congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, then there exists a unique integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accdaf851878abac50b5fc67a58c7674790b8934.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t \\in [0,p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fb1876f7536a4e3b0e06ffae010c167de6939bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(r+t \\cdot p^{k-1}) \\equiv 0 \\pmod {p^k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"226\" height=\"22\" />, given by</li></ol>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0de37d26179b011c0b741b68d2a97322bc2fdaac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[t=-u \\cdot \\frac{f(r)}{p^{k-1}},\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> denotes the inverse of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/c/72cc19e130ba0717b159a2f0822b6ef3796dcc8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p>\n<ol><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/9/a8906dda70ff72ec08e7a5307b1b9b9782aaec92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(r) \\equiv f(r) \\equiv 0 \\pmod {p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"204\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fb1876f7536a4e3b0e06ffae010c167de6939bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(r+t \\cdot p^{k-1}) \\equiv 0 \\pmod {p^k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"226\" height=\"22\" /> for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />.</li></ol>\n<ol><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/5/d35bfc5f459969eaed24a1caedece6b07edc793f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(r) \\equiv 0 \\pmod {p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"20\" /> but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/4/4d404a4bf3e67e6fd88a82c768979219e455e3e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is not congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/0/e40afcf9dc7b212575647ec43a0d272a14bdc2e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) \\equiv 0 \\pmod {p^{k-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"168\" height=\"22\" /> have no solutions with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/f/5ef147e1102a06fadba5f5c2a16d50735ed3d9a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\equiv r \\pmod {p^{k-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"22\" />.</li></ol>\n<p>Each time we bring up the exponent of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, it is said that we have performed a <i>lift</i>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hensel%27s_Lemma&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in the hypothesis, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/5/b35ab48608296e5610c04ee8decd61309a76e1fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(r) \\equiv 0 \\pmod {p^{k-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"22\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/b/8db99a3261aeba6b17548670b2445e79d4d0e4c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r&#39;$\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/4/634d9d89b85bd4b8c9aae0939a5a04e2b7b5909b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(r&#39;) \\equiv 0 \\pmod {p^{k}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"22\" />, then we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/e/bdebef2d9ac31031c81382810e5f547f92e6c939.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r \\equiv r&#39; \\pmod {p^{k-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"22\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/1/3e13664df2d7b761cca98a27732efc86ff7c9967.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r&#39;=r+t \\cdot p^{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"21\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>By the formula for <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Taylor_Series\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Taylor Series\">Taylor Series</a> (of point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c64c92f951891ae17a798629475d8b3c2d25142.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> around the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed47ef35959c171399e8f18eed4b517223823c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a$\" width=\"44\" height=\"8\" />), \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/8/8f8f28d03f7d290bcdcf7071a1194d3de7c79ef7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(a+b)=f(a) +f&#39;(a) \\cdot b + f&#39;&#39;(a) \\cdot \\frac{b^2}{2!} + \\cdot + f^{(n)} (a) \\cdot {b^n}{n!}\\]\" width=\"451\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>We plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/1/0e1489f44949b5da418be8e4f5152aca1d723ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=r$\" width=\"42\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55fef780cb1ee35bf915acaf154ec568b3c1295b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=t \\cdot p^{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"21\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/4/5546bc1367d7a5d9177cac408fcfa19478b1ac55.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(r&#39;)=f(r+t \\cdot p^{k-1})=f(r)+f&#39;(r) \\cdot t \\cdot p^{k-1} + f&#39;&#39;(r) \\cdot \\frac{t^2 \\cdot p^{2k-2}}{2!} + \\dots + f^{(n)} (r) \\cdot \\frac{t^n \\cdot p^{nk-n}}{n!} \\equiv f(r)+f&#39;(r) \\cdot t \\cdot p^{k-1} \\pmod {p^k}\\]\" width=\"885\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>The result for each case follow from the above equation and the conditions of each case. ~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001\" title=\"Ddk001\">Ddk001</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Uses\">Uses</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hensel%27s_Lemma&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Uses\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A great advantage of using this result is that one only have compute (for the most part) inverses modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> instead of higher powers. In fact, one can find inverses of large powers of primes using this result.\n</p><p>Additionally, one can use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chinese_Remainder_Theorem\" title=\"Chinese Remainder Theorem\">Chinese Remainder Theorem</a> to solve polynomial congruences of all moduli.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Example\">Example</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hensel%27s_Lemma&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Example\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the inverse of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65f80dfbc9746e655daa9ad26bf1e7cc378b8593.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$107$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/e/20e5e5c4cb9502ea2f919615a1b96a602fcac17e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$53^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><i>Solution:</i>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the inverse. \n</p><p>Seeing a power of a prime as modulus reminds us of <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Hensel's Lemma</a> for solving polynomial congruences. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/7/50712ba4b2dbfa8fdc730a16384a74e533522bd6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(y)=107y-1\\]\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />. We wish to solve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be2d6c6f8e19aca058a6a6026f8ae4d1a571e30b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(y) \\equiv 0 \\pmod {53^3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"158\" height=\"21\" />. Obviously, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/5/0252e22428dfca6a9f0fcfee1605faeba7a9cb5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$107 \\equiv 1 \\pmod {53}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/b/7dbf093d2154ca364e673a29eb76246965935b9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) \\equiv 0 \\pmod {53}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"20\" />. By <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Hensel's Lemma</a>, there exists a unique integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/c/d5c485a511b95819fe8fee0c437a0176397d623c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t \\in [0,53)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/1/031eef13a733283f5bcbce4677c7e9b0538b87c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(53t+1) \\equiv 0 \\pmod {53^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"205\" height=\"21\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is given by\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/a/f0ad809c2c3ea8e120aa9caa7ad2c4726dd87a5c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[t=- \\bar{f&#39;(1)} \\cdot (\\frac{f(1)}{53})\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/6/e968917a3c00f2cbafb9731f1ed2d2200413df0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bar{f&#39;(1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"22\" /> denotes the inverse of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/1/cc1eda79f76a5b97e34df975296fe955aa089e6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba318f7385187c693cb1859d9b4b1b587e649d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$53$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> (just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba318f7385187c693cb1859d9b4b1b587e649d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$53$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba318f7385187c693cb1859d9b4b1b587e649d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$53$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> to any power). Again, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/5/0252e22428dfca6a9f0fcfee1605faeba7a9cb5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$107 \\equiv 1 \\pmod {53}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />, so since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/426cc5ca6ab7e2e39732151838e18ff514a33b82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(1) =107$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/3/d139825855a3348254e75163478cceeda4bd0814.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bar{f&#39;(1)}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"22\" />, so\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/c/eac21d0da0cfd67fd8a464cf385a3b88b396382b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[t= -1 \\cdot \\frac{106}{53}\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/e/dde465c537623be646a093757de16ec4b7927ec6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=-2\\]\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed0f578693c113d9981a33a9e29e05a1d1ad282.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(-105) \\equiv 0 \\pmod {53^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"190\" height=\"21\" />. We preform another lift. Again, there exists unique integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/c/d5c485a511b95819fe8fee0c437a0176397d623c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t \\in [0,53)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/c/4acc17367aca145373df30ef1dda14d0ebd825d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(-105+53^2 \\cdot t) \\equiv 0 \\pmod {53^3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"258\" height=\"21\" />, given by\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e650b135a687acc6985f55a917004c4a7cc6e5fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[t = - \\bar{f&#39;(-105)} \\cdot (\\frac{f(-105)}{53^2})\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/a/2caa81137c5f29b8101a323cc758142cbad505c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(-105)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"20\" /> is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65f80dfbc9746e655daa9ad26bf1e7cc378b8593.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$107$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/9/4894b3a9db477d37564e516ef23d40e5a3ad6b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bar{f&#39;(-105)} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"22\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/4/cd46b2da87a70bbf9b8ca775de25dd79622f66fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(-105)= -105 \\cdot 107 -1=-106^2= (-4) \\cdot 53^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"379\" height=\"21\" />, so\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/437be237e45cc2845c1855cc93dc0245a7f811b5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[t = -1 \\cdot (\\frac{(-4) \\cdot 53^2}{53^2}\\]\" width=\"152\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/f/46f524dc4b7612e2edc2a2a04de5201767fe9a0a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=4\\]\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f32ae648dbe1b2c3e18fe8d339193d572c7cc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(4 \\cdot 53^2-105) \\equiv 0 \\pmod {53^3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"246\" height=\"21\" />. We have \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/4/7b47d672f0bc6ed89c9ae03704dfa2a2183b5eb0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=\\boxed{4 \\cdot 53^2-105}\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Note that we will use this exact result in the first practice problem.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hensel%27s_Lemma&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introductory\">Introductory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hensel%27s_Lemma&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Introductory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all solutions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f783296fdc83c44c4432f124de2df947d7ef88ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^3-x-1 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{625}\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"20\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/1/15117013d1b9a82a24e57d2e8d7ffa4b5df7bb85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$625$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate\">Intermediate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hensel%27s_Lemma&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the remainder when\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/8/b08715ba212385f09efe9f4fdcc2f5eef8c142ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[106! + (53!)^2\\]\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f6ff7c7f8a4e61c7ef57fe5db49da5d03048c7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$107 \\cdot 53^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"17\" />. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n(<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Problems_Collection\" title=\"Problems Collection\">Source</a>)\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Olympiad\">Olympiad</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hensel%27s_Lemma&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Olympiad\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> there exists an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c9cbfb8d777aeb5018290c1a13e22ee43758b1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3+a-k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.(2014 APMO P3)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hensel%27s_Lemma&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_Theory\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Number Theory\">Number Theory</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Hensel%27s_Lemma&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017234542\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.098 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 471/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 291/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 15741/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.137      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    7.137      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8889:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017234542 and revision id 274097. Rendering wa